From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: D3SOX <nico@d3sox.me>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 23:30:44 +0200
Subject: feat: support native picture-in-picture on Wayland

Use the experimental xx-pip-v1 compositor role when it is advertised, while retaining the existing xdg_toplevel fallback elsewhere. This gives video and Document Picture-in-Picture windows compositor-native stacking and decoration behavior on supported Wayland compositors.

This patch is temporary until the protocol stabilizes and equivalent support can be upstreamed to Chromium.

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/views/overlay/video_overlay_window_views.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/views/overlay/video_overlay_window_views.cc
index 17e13398846104b80fac2f0cda9cd7f6b0753da0..e67d38fa6910caa9a5a54ff07a55b6573da83694 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/views/overlay/video_overlay_window_views.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/views/overlay/video_overlay_window_views.cc
@@ -345,6 +345,7 @@ std::unique_ptr<VideoOverlayWindowViews> VideoOverlayWindowViews::Create(
   // Just to have any non-empty bounds as required by Init(). The window is
   // resized to fit the video that is embedded right afterwards, anyway.
   params.bounds = gfx::Rect(overlay_window->GetMinimumSize());
+  params.is_picture_in_picture = true;
   params.z_order = ui::ZOrderLevel::kFloatingWindow;
   params.visible_on_all_workspaces = true;
   params.remove_standard_frame = true;
